CORE
main.c
--datarace --no-assertions --no-por --unwind 2 --rounds 2 --allow-pointer-unsoundness
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A store through a pointer loaded from the struct it points into becomes a
byte_update of the whole struct at an undecided offset, under the condition
that the pointer targets that struct. Only the leaves the stored bytes meet
may be published as written: leaf[1], which no thread writes after the
spawn, was reported racing (libvsync/hmcslock, no-data-race).
